Core replacement
<UL><LI><b>H01</b> thru <b>H05</b> are connectors that would plug into an existing
8/i computer (in the coresponding sockets) to attempt to substitute a RAM memory for the
core memory.</LI>
<UL>
<LI><b>32KRAM</b> is the whole design on snap-apart paddle cards.</LI>
<LI><b>20230322</b> is a snapshot as of March 22, 2023.</LI>
<LI><b>20230822</b> is a snapshot as of August 22, 2023.</LI>
<LI><b>20230827</b> is a snapshot as of August 27, 2023.</LI>
<LI><b>202405272</b> is a snapshot as of May 27, 2024.</LI>
<LI><b>20240610</b> is a snapshot as of June 10, 2024.</LI>
<LI><b>20240717-7439</b> is a snapshot as of July 17, 2024, using the 7439.</LI>
<LI><b>20240717</b> is a snapshot as of July 17, 2024, using the 7438.</LI>
<LI><b>H01</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H01.</LI>
<LI><b>H02</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H02.</LI>
<LI><b>H03</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H02.</LI>
<LI><b>H04</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H04.</LI>
<LI><b>H05-dl</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H05 using delay lines.</LI>
<LI><b>H05X1</b> is a drawing of the board for slot H05 using monostables.</LI>
</UL>
